{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.node.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "tsBuildInfoFile": "./node_modules/.tmp/tsconfig.services.tsbuildinfo",
    "types": ["node", "vitest/globals"],
    /* The service imports src/lib/*.ts by relative path and Node runs it through
       tsx, so extensionless TS imports resolve the same way Vite resolves them
       for the app. */
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    /* The shared packages the service imports, resolved to source.

       Absent until API ticket 07, which is why `@imani/wallet-core` had been
       reporting TS2307 here for as long as the service has existed: the service
       is RUN by tsx, which resolves these through vite.config's aliases, and
       typechecked by a project that could not.

       Adding them fixes five TS2307s and reveals what those were masking —
       once the modules resolve, their types apply, and the service's tests
       stop being `unknown`. That is a real backlog rather than a regression,
       and it is now visible instead of hidden behind an unresolved import.
       Two non-test errors in `server.ts` predate this and are unrelated to
       any package. */
    "baseUrl": ".",
    "paths": {
      "@imani/wallet-core": ["./packages/wallet-core/src/index.ts"],
      "@imani/reports": ["./packages/reports/src/index.ts"],
      "@imani/redemption": ["./packages/redemption/src/index.ts"],
      "@imani/voucher-send": ["./packages/voucher-send/src/index.ts"],
      "@imani/wallet-storage": ["./packages/wallet-storage/src/index.ts"]
    }
  },
  /* `src/lib/audit.ts` is included, not just referenced: the audit API's whole
     point is that it runs the SAME reader the wallet does, so a change there
     that breaks the service must fail this build rather than the deployment.

     The service reads the kind and version from `src/lib/attestationKind.ts`,
     which is pulled in automatically as an import of audit.ts. It does NOT
     import `attestation.ts`: the producer reaches `./nap` and `./relay`, hence
     `@imani/nap-client-web` and `import.meta.env` — a browser dependency graph
     and a Vite-only global that no Node service has. That split is also why the
     API physically cannot sign an attestation. */
  "include": ["services", "src/lib/audit.ts"]
}
